    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-08-28T05:08:30+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-28T05:08:30+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-27T19:38:30Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-27T19:38:30Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system over NSW will weaken and merge with another high pressure system to the south of SA today as a low pressure trough hovers over WA close to the SA border. The high to the south will move slowly east over the weekend to be centred over Victoria by Monday, strengthening a ridge over South Australia into next week.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW010" description="West Coast" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-08-28T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-29T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-27T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-28T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers west of Ceduna, becoming less likely in the evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Nullarbor in the morning and afternoon. Thunderstorms possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding west of Nullarbor in the afternoon and evening. Winds north to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending east to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h in the late afternoon then becoming light in the evening. Daytime maximum temperatures in the low to mid 20s.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 10:00am to 3:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 5 [Moderate]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-08-29T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-30T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-28T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-29T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower west of Nullarbor, most likely in the late afternoon and evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Winds northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h turning easterly 15 to 20 km/h in the middle of the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 12 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-08-30T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-31T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-29T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-30T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h becoming light during the afternoon then becoming easterly 15 to 20 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 11 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-08-31T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-01T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-30T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-31T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending north to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to around 9 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to high 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
